# PX4 EKF2 parameters for GPS-denied flight on external vision.
# Format: <vehicle_id> <component_id> <name> <value> <type>  (type 6 = int32, 9 = float)
# These are a STARTING POINT — tune EV delay/noise to your VIO/VTRN pipeline.
#
# HOW TO APPLY THIS FILE
#   QGroundControl: Vehicle Setup > Parameters > Tools > Load from file, then reboot.
#   Headless / pxh console: this text format is QGC's, NOT PX4's. `param load` and
#   `param import` in pxh read *BSON* and fail on this file with a tinybson
#   "node name overflow" as they try to parse these comments. Generate console
#   commands instead:
#       droneflight px4-params --file configs/px4/gps_denied_ekf2.params \
#                              --file configs/px4/sitl_bringup.params
#   and paste the `param set` lines into pxh, then `reboot`.
#
# Pairs with `droneflight ev-bridge`, which supplies the vision pose. In SITL,
# apply sitl_bringup.params as well.

# External-vision fusion bitmask: 1 = horizontal position, 2 = vertical position,
# 4 = velocity, 8 = yaw.  11 = position (H+V) + yaw, which is exactly what
# VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE carries. That message has no velocity field, so bit 2
# (i.e. 15) would ask EKF2 to fuse something the bridge never sends; set it only
# if you switch to ODOMETRY with a populated twist.
1	1	EKF2_EV_CTRL	11	6
# Disable all GPS fusion (0 = no GPS aiding) — this is what makes the run
# GPS-denied. It also means EKF2 gets no global origin from GNSS, so `ev-bridge`
# sends SET_GPS_GLOBAL_ORIGIN (the plan's home); without that a lat/lon mission
# cannot be flown at all. See RUNBOOK §3b.
1	1	EKF2_GPS_CTRL	0	6
# Height reference: 0 = barometer, 1 = GPS, 2 = range sensor, 3 = vision.
# 3 keeps height on the same source as position; fall back to 0 (baro) if the EV
# height is noisy. NOTE: the bridge injects horizontal error only, so EV height
# is ground truth here — height performance is NOT being tested.
1	1	EKF2_HGT_REF	3	6
# External-vision measurement delay (ms) — set to your pipeline's latency.
# With `ev-bridge --timestamp none` PX4 stamps on receipt, so this parameter is
# the only thing modelling pipeline lag; a real VIO/VTRN stack is tens of ms behind.
1	1	EKF2_EV_DELAY	50	9
# Allow arming without a GPS lock (GPS-denied ops).
1	1	COM_ARM_WO_GPS	1	6
# Low-altitude / nap-of-the-earth: keep the mission altitude modest (m, relative).
1	1	MIS_TAKEOFF_ALT	5	9
